From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 21:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a popup is drawn inside the window it opened over

Clicking a <select> on a tty opened nothing anyone could see. The list is a
page popup: `RenderWidgetHostViewAura::InitAsPopup` makes an aura window of
`WINDOW_TYPE_MENU` and hands it to `ParentWindowWithContext`, and
`DesktopNativeWidgetAuraWindowParentingClient::GetDefaultParent` answers a
menu with a top-level widget of its own. A views menu -- a context menu -- and
a tooltip take the same road from the other end: `GetNativeWidgetTypeForInitParams`
answers `TYPE_MENU` and `TYPE_TOOLTIP` with `kDesktopNativeWidgetAura` even
when they have a parent.

On ozone/drm a second top-level window binds to no CRTC -- `0023` says why,
and set `presents_every_window` false for it -- so every frame such a window
submits is dropped. The popup opened, took the capture and the keyboard, and
was never drawn.

ChromeOS never meets this because ash keeps menus inside the root window. So
does this, on the platforms that say they need it: both places ask
`presents_every_window`, and where the answer is no a menu stays a child of the
window it belongs to and is drawn in that window's frame. Every other platform
answers yes and is untouched. What is lost is a menu leaving its window, which
on a tty is leaving the screen.

`scripts/test-a-popup-is-drawn-inside-its-window.sh` reads the series for both
halves.
---
 .../ui/views/chrome_views_delegate_linux.cc   | 10 ++++++++
 .../desktop_native_widget_aura.cc             | 25 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 35 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/views/chrome_views_delegate_linux.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/views/chrome_views_delegate_linux.cc
index c5808a0797..c7a7a46e0f 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/views/chrome_views_delegate_linux.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/views/chrome_views_delegate_linux.cc
@@ -86,6 +86,16 @@ NativeWidgetType GetNativeWidgetTypeForInitParams(
     return NativeWidgetType::kDesktopNativeWidgetAura;
   }
 
+  // Domicile's engine fork. A menu or tooltip is a top-level window of its own
+  // so that it can leave its parent's bounds, but on a platform that presents
+  // only the window filling a display that window is never drawn: on ozone/drm
+  // it binds to no CRTC. Draw it in its parent instead, as ash does.
+  if (params.parent && !ui::OzonePlatform::GetInstance()
+                            ->GetPlatformRuntimeProperties()
+                            .presents_every_window) {
+    return NativeWidgetType::kNativeWidgetAura;
+  }
+
   return (params.parent &&
           params.type != views::Widget::InitParams::TYPE_MENU &&
           params.type != views::Widget::InitParams::TYPE_TOOLTIP)
diff --git a/ui/views/widget/desktop_aura/desktop_native_widget_aura.cc b/ui/views/widget/desktop_aura/desktop_native_widget_aura.cc
index c79a1ab2ba..4bb10fd169 100644
--- a/ui/views/widget/desktop_aura/desktop_native_widget_aura.cc
+++ b/ui/views/widget/desktop_aura/desktop_native_widget_aura.cc
@@ -88,6 +88,10 @@
 #include "ui/wm/core/window_properties.h"
 #endif
 
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_OZONE)
+#include "ui/ozone/public/ozone_platform.h"
+#endif
+
 DEFINE_EXPORTED_UI_CLASS_PROPERTY_TYPE(VIEWS_EXPORT,
                                        views::DesktopNativeWidgetAura*)
 
@@ -99,6 +103,18 @@ DEFINE_UI_CLASS_PROPERTY_KEY(DesktopNativeWidgetAura*,
 
 namespace {
 
+// Whether a top-level window of its own can reach a display at all. See
+// PlatformRuntimeProperties::presents_every_window.
+bool PlatformPresentsEveryWindow() {
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_OZONE)
+  return ui::OzonePlatform::GetInstance()
+      ->GetPlatformRuntimeProperties()
+      .presents_every_window;
+#else
+  return true;
+#endif
+}
+
 // This class provides functionality to create a top level widget to host a
 // child window.
 class DesktopNativeWidgetTopLevelHandler : public aura::WindowObserver {
@@ -259,6 +275,15 @@ class DesktopNativeWidgetAuraWindowParentingClient
                          ui::mojom::WindowShowState::kFullscreen;
     bool is_menu = window->GetType() == aura::client::WINDOW_TYPE_MENU;
 
+    // Domicile's engine fork. On a platform that presents only the window
+    // filling a display, a menu's own top-level window is never drawn: on
+    // ozone/drm it binds to no CRTC, so a <select>'s list or a context menu
+    // opened invisible. Keep it in this root window instead, as ash does, so
+    // it is drawn in the frame of the window it opened over.
+    if (is_menu && !PlatformPresentsEveryWindow()) {
+      return root_window_;
+    }
+
     if (is_fullscreen || is_menu) {
       ui::ZOrderLevel root_z_order = ui::ZOrderLevel::kNormal;
       internal::NativeWidgetPrivate* native_widget =
